            <div xml:id="d277">

                <pb facs="0290" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/864</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-09-29T16:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 29, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 1, 2.45
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1763. McNally sends the following:</p>
                <p>The President’s reply to the peace note of the Pope has had a great effect in the
                    better as well as in the lower German circles where the <pb facs="0291" n="217"
                        xml:id="pg217"/> true text is known. Great unrest among the working classes
                    is causing the German Government very great anxiety and naval and military
                    officials have been instructed to be prepared to cope with any threatening
                    demonstration. At a very recent meeting called by the Kaiser at which Hindenburg
                    and the leaders among the naval and Government officers were present the German
                    Emperor informed his guests that if it was the desire of the Army, Navy, and the
                    people of Germany that he abdicate he would do so. All present pledged their
                    loyalty, offered their general support of his dynasty.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
